While testing the new adhoc tasks implemented as part of [https://moodle.atlassian.net/browse/MDL-81015|https://moodle.atlassian.net/browse/MDL-81015|smart-link] it’s been found that it’s possible to hit AWS SNS rate limit when sending SMS in bulk. For example the following error is hitting the hard rate for {{SetSMSAttributes}}:

Error code from AWS SNS: {{Throttling. Exception message: Error executing "SetSMSAttributes" on "https://sns.region.amazonaws.com"; AWS HTTP error: Client error: POST https://sns.region.amazonaws.com resulted in a 400 Bad Request response: Sender Throttling< (truncated...) Throttling (client): Rate exceeded - Sender Throttling Rate exceeded}}

It would be great to resend those messages automatically.

Some actions in the XMLDB editor generate upgrade.php code that can be run twice, in case there were issues before the savepoint. For adding and removing fields we have this kind of guard clause:

{noformat}if (!$dbman->field_exists($table, $field)) {
    $dbman->add_field($table, $field);
}{noformat}

I suggest we do this for renaming fields too, since it is a simple check to just confirm the {{$field}} still exists like so:

{noformat}if ($dbman->field_exists($table, $field)) {
    $dbman->rename_field($table, $field, 'newfieldname');
}{noformat}

This will help a lot when upgrades inevitably fail, and an upgrade must be retried.

Currently Moodle will always create a cookie session unless you use the {{NO_MOODLE_COOKIES}} constant, which you define before including {{config.php}}.

This has worked okay for many years and is primarily used by things like:

* {{theme/styles.php}}
* {{theme/javascript.php}}
* {{lib/requirejs.php}}
* {{lib/editor/tiny/lang.php}}
* {{service-nologin.php}}

This is important in the above cases because:

* we do not need to start a session
* a session incurs additional overhead



Working on the Moodle Router, we want to make it as fast and lightweight as possible so that, when we come to migrate things like the above endpoints, we do not have any additional overhead that they currently do not have.

We already have a reduced bootstrap using the {{ABORT_AFTER_CONFIG}} constant to exit before initially connecting to the database, but we also need to provide a solution for session cookies.

I propose that we:

* keep the existing {{NO_MOODLE_COOKIES}} constant and respect if it is set during initial bootstrap
* update the session manager to add:
** a new flag for {{bool $supportscookies}}
** a setter to change the flag
* update {{lib/setup.php}} to set the flag based on the initial value of the constant

This will allow us to set the router to not support cookies, but for them to be enabled at a later point and a session to be started. This is currently _not_ possible.

This issue tracks the implementation of improved, linear navigation for course content by *eliminating separate subsection pages* and consolidating content onto the main section pages.

h2. 💡 Research and discovery decisions

Based on research into the desired course linear navigation experience, the following architectural and UX decisions were made:

* *Subsection pages removal:* Dedicated subsection view pages are being removed from Moodle LMS. However, the existing functionality to display subsection content must be retained within {{section.php}} to maintain compatibility with third-party plugins.
* *Subsection links update:*
** Links to subsections will remain in the *breadcrumbs* and the *course index*.
** These links will now use *anchor links* (jump links) to navigate directly to the respective subsection _within_ the main Section page.

h2. ✅ Implementation tasks

This issue should implement the following changes:

# *Update navigation links:* Modify links in the following areas to point to the relevant anchor on the main section page:
#* Breadcrumbs
#* Course index
#* Permalink action
#* Subsection link
# *Remove 'View' Action:* Remove the *View* action from the subsection menu in edit mode, as there is no longer a separate page to view.
# *Display subsections inline* when the layout is set to “Show one section per page”.

h2. 🛠️ Technical implementation notes

The following methods and files need modification to implement the required URL changes:

h3. 1. Updating the permalink action

The *permalink* for a subsection must be updated to link to the section page, using the subsection's number as an anchor.

* *File:* {{public/course/format/classes/output/local/content/cm/delegatedcontrolmenu.php}}
* *Method:* {{get_section_permalink_item()}}

{noformat}$parentsection = $this->mod->get_section_info();
$url = new url(
    '/course/section.php',
    ['id' => $parentsection->id],
    'section-' . $this->section->sectionnum,
);{noformat}



h3. 2. Updating breadcrumbs, course index, and subsection link

The function responsible for generating the view URL for sections needs to be updated to consistently return the URL for the parent section page when a delegated subsection is being referenced.

* *Example File:* {{public/course/format/topics/lib.php}}
* *Function:* {{get_view_url()}}

{noformat}    if ((!empty($options['navigation']) || array_key_exists('sr', $options)) && $sectionno !== null) {
        $sectioninfo = $this->get_section($sectionno);
        if ($sectioninfo->is_delegated()) {
            // Delegated sections are handled differently.
            $parent = $sectioninfo->get_component_instance()->get_parent_section();
            return new core\\url(
                '/course/section.php',
                ['id' => $parent->id],
                'section-' . $sectionno,
            );
        }
        // Display section on separate page.
        return new moodle_url('/course/section.php', ['id' => $sectioninfo->id]);
    }{noformat}



➕ More information can be found in [https://moodle.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/Moppies/pages/3390144515/Remove+subsections+page|https://moodle.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/Moppies/pages/3390144515/Remove+subsections+page|smart-link]

This issue tracks the implementation of improved, linear navigation for course content by *removing the description field for subsections*.

h2. 💡 Research and discovery decisions

Based on research into the desired course linear navigation experience, the following architectural and UX decisions were made:

* *Subsection descriptions removed:* Support for subsection descriptions will be *discontinued*. The subsection settings page will be streamlined to contain only the *Name* and *Restrict access*.

h2. ✅ Implementation tasks

This issue should implement the following changes:

# *Remove description from settings page:* The *Description* field should be removed from the *Subsection* settings page:
!image-20251124-080350.png|width=640,alt="image-20251124-080350.png"!
The description must be kept on the Section settings page.


h2. 🛠️ Technical implementation notes

The following methods and files need modification to implement the required URL changes:

h3. 1. Eliminating the Description field from the settings page

* *File:* {{public/course/editsection_form.php}}
* Display the ‘summary_editor’ only for non-delegated sections:

{noformat}    if (!$sectioninfo->is_delegated()) {
        $mform->addElement('editor', 'summary_editor', get_string('description'), null, $this->_customdata['editoroptions']);
        $mform->setType('summary_editor', PARAM_RAW);
    }{noformat}

 



➕ More information can be found in [https://moodle.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/Moppies/pages/3390144515/Remove+subsections+page|https://moodle.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/Moppies/pages/3390144515/Remove+subsections+page|smart-link]
